To fix the CORS error in WordPress when using Next.js, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the `cors` package in your Next.js project by running `npm install cors`.
2. In your `next.config.js` file, add the following configuration to enable CORS:
```javascript
module.exports = {
  // ...
  async headers() {
    return [
      {
        source: '/api/:path*',
        headers: [
          { key: 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', value: 'true' },
          { key: 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin', value: 'https://your-wordpress-site.com' },
          { key: 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods', value: 'GET,OPTIONS,PATCH,DELETE,POST' },
          { key: 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers', value: 'X-CSRF-Token, X-Requested-With, Accept, Accept-Version, Content-Length, Content-MD5, Content-Type, Date, X-Api-Version' },
        ],
      },
    ];
  },
};
```
Replace `https://your-wordpress-site.com` with the URL of your WordPress site.
3. In your WordPress site, add the following code to your `wp-config.php` file to enable CORS:
```php
add_filter('rest_allow_origins', function ($allow) {
  $allow = array_merge($allow, array('https://your-nextjs-site.com'));
  return $allow;
});
```
Replace `https://your-nextjs-site.com` with the URL of your Next.js site.
4. Save both files and refresh your browser. You should now be able to make API requests from your Next.js app to your WordPress site without encountering the CORS error.

