4. Create a `Visualizer` class that will handle the visualization of the audio waveform.
5. Implement the `Visualizer` class to draw the waveform on a `Texture2D` object.
6. Update the `Visualizer` class in real-time to reflect changes in the audio waveform.
7. Attach the `Visualizer` class to the same GameObject as the `AudioSource` component.
8. Adjust the settings of the `Visualizer` class to customize the appearance of the visualizer.
9. Test your script by playing the audio file and observing the visualizer in action.

